<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 16-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 16-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Opal, with 40 mph winds, is in the eastern Philippine Sea near 15.4n/132.7e, nearly stationary. It will intensify to a typhoon with 80 mph winds within 48 hours. Opal will begin a slow north northwest movement during this period, threatening shipping.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
</text>
